@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.TeamAlifModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Alif";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team">← Back</a>
        </div>

        <div class="event-hero reveal">
            <div class="event-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Our Team</p>
                <h2>Alif</h2>

                <p class="event-intro">
                    A barista who continues to grow through practice, passion, and
                    consistency—especially in the art he enjoys most: latte art.
                </p>

                <div class="event-tags">
                    <span>Barista</span>
                    <span>Latte Art</span>
                    <span>Craft & Service</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="team-profile-hero-img reveal">
                <img src="/images/team/alif.jpg" alt="Alif">
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-block reveal">
            <div class="hbii-block-text">
                <p class="hbii-label">His Journey</p>
                <h3>A Space to Keep Growing</h3>

                <p>
                    Alif joined Kopi Cinta in 2024. Although he already had experience
                    in the coffee field, this is where he found a space to continue
                    learning and growing.
                </p>

                <p>
                    As a barista, he is always looking to improve his skills—
                    especially in latte art, which he enjoys the most.
                </p>

                <p>
                    For him, growth is not something instant. It is something built
                    over time, through consistency and dedication.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-block-card">
                <h4>His Focus</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Barista craft</li>
                    <li>Latte art development</li>
                    <li>Customer interaction</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-feature reveal">
            <div class="hbii-feature-card">
                <p class="hbii-label">Practice</p>
                <h3>Every Moment is a Chance to Improve</h3>

                <p>
                    When there are no orders, Alif uses the time to practice on his own.
                    And when there are orders, he treats each one as an opportunity
                    to improve his skills directly.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Through this process, he is able to see his progress over time—
                    and that is what keeps him motivated.
                </p>

                <p>
                    He feels happy to be here, because he can continue learning
                    while doing something he truly enjoys.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-feature-card soft">
                <p class="hbii-label">Challenge</p>
                <h3>When Communication Becomes Difficult</h3>

                <p>
                    One of the challenges Alif often faces is communication with customers,
                    especially when they wear masks, making it difficult for him to
                    read lip movements.
                </p>

                <p>
                    To handle this, he usually asks customers to repeat, uses gestures,
                    or invites them to point directly at the menu.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-ending reveal">
            <h3>His Message</h3>

            <p>
                Alif hopes customers can speak more clearly, avoid covering their mouth,
                or simply point at the menu—because it helps communication a lot.
            </p>

            <p>
                Thank you for your understanding. He hopes every interaction can become
                a moment to learn together.
            </p>

            <p>
                Because for him, every cup is not just about taste—
                but about process, growth, and connection.
            </p>
        </div>

        <br />

        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Team</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>